# config/liveness-resume - the OPTIONAL relaunch command for the external
# liveness watchdog (bin/fm-liveness-watchdog.sh). Copy this into a local,
# gitignored config/liveness-resume and edit.
#
# The watchdog always re-wakes the primary's recorded supervisor pane
# (state/.supervisor-target) when the primary dies with work in flight: a
# live-but-idle pane gets a gentle Enter nudge with NO config needed. This file
# is only for the harder case - a supervisor pane that reads as a DEAD shell (the
# client process is truly gone, not just idle). When that happens AND this file
# exists, the watchdog runs this single command IN that pane via the backend's
# text-submit to relaunch the client.
#
# When config/liveness-resume is ABSENT, a dead client is escalated for MANUAL
# recovery but never relaunched. A live-but-idle pane is unaffected either way.
#
# This command is HOST/RUNTIME-SPECIFIC: it is however this host relaunches the
# firstmate primary in its own pane. Keep any secret it needs in this gitignored
# file, never committed.
#
# The watchdog caps attempts (FM_LIVENESS_MAX_RESUMES, default 3) within one
# down-episode and then escalates instead of retrying forever, so this command
# does not need its own loop or backoff.
#
# Example (illustrative - replace with this host's real relaunch line): resume
# the jcode primary session by its recorded id.
jcode --resume "$(cat "$FM_HOME/state/.primary-session-id" 2>/dev/null)"
